Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:05.00,Header,,0,0,0,0,This is a Gentlemen of the Hàn free fansub.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.86,0:00:05.58,Episode Title,,0,0,0,0,{\fade(255,0,255,0,1025,3900,4700)\pos(653.755,324.22)}Episode 74
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.86,0:00:05.58,Episode Title,,0,0,0,0,{\fade(255,0,255,0,1025,3900,4700)\pos(653.755,494.455)}Zhuge Posing as a God
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.78,0:00:34.40,Default,,0,0,0,,If not for your rescue, \Nmy life would have been over.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.40,0:00:37.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhongda, how did you know about my great defeat?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.95,0:00:40.58,Default,,0,0,0,,The Shu withdrew their ambush of Ji Gorge,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.58,0:00:42.78,Default,,0,0,0,,so they must have tried to attack Xie Gorge.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.78,0:00:45.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I feared for you, so I came to assist,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.05,0:00:47.95,Default,,0,0,0,,and it was mere coincidence that I encountered you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.50,0:00:52.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhongda, your strategic mind is truly something I cannot match.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.08,0:00:57.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander, you are too modest.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.65,0:01:03.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Now after such a devastating defeat, we have lost the camp.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.70,0:01:03.02,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,3900,4300)\pos(337.333,462.667)}Cáo Zhēn\NStyled: Zǐdān
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.31,0:01:05.50,Default,,0,0,0,,What shall we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.83,0:01:11.85,Default,,0,0,0,,With Zhuge Liang opening a path through Mount Qi, our army will struggle to hold ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.30,0:01:16.22,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,5500,5900)\pos(993,480.667)}Sīmǎ Yì\NStyled: Zhòngdá
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.64,0:01:18.13,Default,,0,0,0,,We must set up camp at Weiyin and strategize further.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.71,0:01:25.86,Default,,0,0,0,,This defeat lies on my shoulders alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.86,0:01:28.20,Default,,0,0,0,,I have failed the Emperor's trust.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.17,0:01:33.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow, I shall offer the jade belt to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.70,0:01:37.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander, why are you taking this so seriously?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.46,0:01:39.81,Default,,0,0,0,,The wager was simply but a mere jest.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.81,0:01:42.99,Default,,0,0,0,,It was to show our shared commitment to serving our nation.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.65,0:01:51.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, it was General Wei who ordered me to advance!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.54,0:01:52.42,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(982.333,496.667)}Wèi Yán\NStyled: Wéncháng
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.70,0:01:55.32,Default,,0,0,0,,It was General Wei who ordered me to advance! Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.42,0:01:54.26,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(345,490.667)}Zhūgě Liàng\NStyled: Kǒngmíng
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.32,0:01:57.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.26,0:02:04.85,Default,,0,0,0,,It was General Wei who rescued you from the encirclement, and you now accuse him?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.85,0:02:07.23,Default,,0,0,0,,There are no excuses for disobedience.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.23,0:02:08.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Execute him!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.30,0:02:09.86,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(997,489)}Chén Shì
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.34,0:02:13.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, Chancellor, it was General Wei who ordered me to advance!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.05,0:02:17.20,Default,,0,0,0,,It was General Wei who ordered me to advance, Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.67,0:02:32.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, Cao Zhen is bedridden and is currently recuperating in the camp.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.54,0:02:42.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Summon the two surrendered Wei soldiers to come before me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.66,0:02:43.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.57,0:02:47.07,Default,,0,0,0,,-Bring brush, ink, paper, and inkstone.\N-Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.63,0:03:01.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Greetings, Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.73,0:03:09.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Your families are mostly still in the Central Plains.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.77,0:03:12.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, I am letting you return home.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.19,0:03:14.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.05,0:03:17.67,Default,,0,0,0,,There is but one task that I need you to complete.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.81,0:03:22.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I have written a letter here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.23,0:03:29.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I want you to take it back to the Wei camp and deliver it to Commander Cao.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.69,0:03:32.30,Default,,0,0,0,,We will do as you say. Rest assured, Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.81,0:03:50.48,Thinking,,0,0,0,,In his letter, Zhuge Liang mocked \NCao Zhen for his lack of education.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.48,0:03:53.44,Thinking,,0,0,0,,For his constant defeats, \Nhe deemed him unfit to command.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.44,0:03:56.49,Thinking,,0,0,0,,"What face do you have left to face the people of Guanzhong?"
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.49,0:04:00.28,Thinking,,0,0,0,,"What honor do you have to return to the Chancellor's manor?"
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.28,0:04:06.14,Thinking,,0,0,0,,After reading it, his chest filled with anger, and he died in the army camp that night.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.05,0:04:05.00,Default,,0,0,0,,-Zhuge... you peasant!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.37,0:04:15.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Peasant Zhuge...!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.14,0:04:36.80,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(1001.143,481.143)}Liú Shàn\NStyled: Gòngsì
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.49,0:04:42.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, it's you again! Again!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.92,0:04:50.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Who…Who could it be?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.38,0:04:52.09,Default,,0,0,0,,It's you!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.09,0:04:55.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.64,0:04:59.52,Default,,0,0,0,,The Chancellor's messenger has arrived, asking about the grain supplies.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.22,0:05:02.82,Default,,0,0,0,,We've already sent someone to deliver it!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.22,0:05:19.54,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,6980,7300)\pos(1008,456)}Yáng Yí\NStyled: Wēigōng
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.82,0:05:15.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.77,0:05:19.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Li Yan of Yong'an has sent District Lieutenant Gou An
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.47,0:05:22.18,Default,,0,0,0,,to escort the grain and deliver it to the army.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.18,0:05:26.01,Default,,0,0,0,,However, because of his fondness for wine, \Nhe has been ten days late.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.74,0:05:31.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Summon Gou An into the tent.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.59,0:05:34.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Summon Gou An into the tent!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.98,0:05:43.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Spare me, Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.05,0:05:47.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Grain is of utmost importance to the army.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.63,0:05:49.82,Default,,0,0,0,,A three day delay is punishable by death.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.82,0:05:51.28,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(298,473)}Gǒu Ān
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.30,0:05:54.78,Default,,0,0,0,,You dared to drink along the way, resulting in a ten day delay.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.78,0:05:56.14,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you have to say?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.53,0:05:59.22,Default,,0,0,0,,-Men. \N-Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.22,0:06:00.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Execute him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.43,0:06:00.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.57,0:06:05.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, spare me!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.40,0:06:07.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.12,0:06:10.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Gou An was under Li Yan's command. It would be unwise to execute him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.30,0:06:20.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Most of our grain comes from the Western Riverlands.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.94,0:06:25.87,Default,,0,0,0,,If you kill this man, I fear that no one will dare transport grain in the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.75,0:06:36.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Spare his life for now, but beat him eighty times.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.62,0:06:39.25,Default,,0,0,0,,If he delays again, there will be no mercy.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.25,0:06:44.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.09,0:07:28.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhuge Liang is skilled in strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.31,0:07:35.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I find it hard to believe that you are truly surrendering to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.76,0:07:41.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I, Gou An, am sincerely surrendering, with no hidden motives at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.64,0:07:43.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that so?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.87,0:07:50.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Would you be willing to do a significant task for me?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.88,0:07:52.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course! Of course!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.70,0:07:55.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Please...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.54,0:08:01.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, Commander, command me. I, Gou An, will serve you!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.33,0:08:07.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Return to Chengdu and spread rumors.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.19,0:08:11.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Say that Zhuge Liang harbors resentment towards the throne,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.18,0:08:13.15,Default,,0,0,0,,and that he intends to usurp it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.40,0:08:17.84,Default,,0,0,0,,This will compel Liu Shan to recall Zhuge Liang.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.72,0:08:22.67,Default,,0,0,0,,If this succeeds, I will report it to the Emperor,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.67,0:08:25.24,Default,,0,0,0,,and have you promoted and ennobled.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.99,0:08:30.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I will carry out your orders, Commander, with all my power!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.45,0:08:31.92,Default,,0,0,0,,All my strength!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.80,0:08:36.82,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Oh, what to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.06,0:08:39.00,Thinking,,0,0,0,,The Chancellor...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.32,0:08:40.36,Thinking,,0,0,0,,What do you think...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.78,0:08:42.80,Thinking,,0,0,0,,This won't do!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.52,0:08:44.60,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Need to do this now...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.60,0:08:45.28,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Go and say it...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.26,0:08:50.18,Thinking,,0,0,0,,This matter... Rumors...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.14,0:08:59.03,Default,,0,0,0,,If the Chancellor truly harbors such ambitions, what could be done then?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.69,0:09:03.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.08,0:09:08.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}The Chancellor has become \Nprideful over his achievements;
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.69,0:09:10.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}he will usurp the throne sooner or later.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.24,0:09:21.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}Your Majesty, in my humble opinion, please issue an edict immediately
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.40,0:09:24.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}to recall Zhuge Liang back to Chengdu.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.26,0:09:28.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}Then, strip him of any command to forestall a future revolt!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.88,0:09:34.90,Default,,0,0,0,,What you say has merit.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.12,0:09:40.67,Default,,0,0,0,,This is our fourth expedition out of Mount Qi, and our first battle has been a victory.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.67,0:09:45.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Sima Yi's forces were defeated at the \NWei River; this is a Heaven-sent opportunity!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.47,0:09:50.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Our forces will press forward, not giving the enemy any chance to breathe.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.18,0:09:51.42,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,"Restore the Central Plains"
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.71,0:09:54.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope that all the officers and soldiers will fight with all their might,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.59,0:09:58.69,Default,,0,0,0,,and, with one push, cross the Wei River and take Chang'an!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.69,0:10:02.38,Default,,0,0,0,,The restoration of the Central Plains is within reach!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.07,0:10:03.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Jiang Wei.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.64,0:10:07.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.73,0:10:11.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Lead 30,000 elite soldiers around the Wei River to the rear of the Wei camps
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.15,0:10:13.78,Default,,0,0,0,,and cut off Sima Yi's route back to Chang'an.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.77,0:10:17.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Hear the edict of our lord Liu Shan!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.51,0:10:38.99,Default,,0,0,0,,His Majesty has decreed...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.86,0:10:47.60,Default,,0,0,0,,I was to return with triumph, but the \Nimperial decree bade me return to court.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.34,0:10:54.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, our army has won all engagements. Now is the time to advance right towards Chang'an.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.29,0:10:55.71,Default,,0,0,0,,How can we retreat halfway?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.06,0:11:02.07,Default,,0,0,0,,The Emperor is young. He may have been...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.84,0:11:09.96,Default,,0,0,0,,If I do not return, I would disobey the decree and betray my lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.49,0:11:14.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet, if I retreat, we may miss the perfect opportunity...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.50,0:11:23.54,Default,,0,0,0,,...and we may never find such a chance again.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.79,0:11:37.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.24,0:11:49.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Issue the order, withdraw the army.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.66,0:11:54.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.97,0:12:37.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander, this camp has two thousand more stoves than the previous camps.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.13,0:12:44.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Order the army not to pursue the \NShu forces and to return immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.57,0:12:46.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander, why is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.61,0:12:52.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Though Zhuge Liang is full of schemes, he has shown a flaw.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.73,0:12:57.30,Default,,0,0,0,,He increases his soldiers and stoves each day, a set up to an ambush,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.30,0:13:01.13,Default,,0,0,0,,to lure us into pursuit and surround us.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.13,0:13:03.74,Default,,0,0,0,,As the commander, how could I fall for such a trap?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.74,0:13:05.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Withdraw the troops.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.18,0:13:05.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.18,0:13:10.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Transmit the commander's order to withdraw all troops.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.39,0:13:21.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Father-Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.32,0:13:27.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I, your old servant, led troops out of Mount Qi and defeated the Wei army many times.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.78,0:13:32.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I intended to advance on Chang'an, but suddenly received Your Majesty's edict,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.14,0:13:37.65,Default,,0,0,0,,which called me back to Chengdu from a thousand {\i1}li {\i0}away.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.65,0:13:39.81,Default,,0,0,0,,How great would the matter at hand be?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.81,0:13:41.94,Default,,0,0,0,,It...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.24,0:13:51.56,Default,,0,0,0,,It's because We have missed your presence, so We summoned you back.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.56,0:13:54.45,Default,,0,0,0,,It's for nothing else. Father-Chancellor, please rise.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.39,0:13:57.33,Default,,0,0,0,,For this alone?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.32,0:14:01.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes! Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.01,0:14:03.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}I believe that there is a reason behind this,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.23,0:14:06.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}and that this is not Your Majesty's own intent.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.30,0:14:20.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}There must have been a treacherous official who claimed that I have ulterior motives.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.48,0:14:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}Your old servant was greatly favored by the\N late emperor and I swore to repay it with my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.00,0:14:36.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}Thus, I have led numerous northern expeditions
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.69,0:14:41.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}to punish evil and revive the House of Han.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.08,0:14:45.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}On the battlefield, I have fought to the death,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.03,0:14:47.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}and the troops were willing to risk their lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.81,0:14:51.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}At the front, I have moved troops and used generals,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.05,0:14:53.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}not daring to neglect my duties.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.12,0:14:58.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}Now, after marching out of Mount Qi,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.21,0:15:01.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}I have defeated Sima Yi and the Wei army many times,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.37,0:15:03.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}and a great opportunity showed itself!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.64,0:15:06.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}As the late emperor's last will was about to be fulfilled,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.96,0:15:10.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}Your Majesty has heeded slander
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.74,0:15:14.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}and issued an edict to recall the troops.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.50,0:15:17.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}Should the late emperor hear of this in the afterlife,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.85,0:15:21.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}would his heart not be broken?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.41,0:15:26.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.05,0:15:36.91,Default,,0,0,0,,It was We who wrongly heeded the advice of Our eunuch and recalled you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.91,0:15:38.70,Default,,0,0,0,,We regret it greatly.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.54,0:15:47.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Who put forward such a suggestion to His Majesty?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.08,0:15:55.44,Default,,0,0,0,,It was I who believed in the rumors.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.70,0:15:59.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Rumors from where?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.04,0:16:04.05,Default,,0,0,0,,It was Gou An the grain escort who said that.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.05,0:16:05.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Gou An?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.41,0:16:06.64,Default,,0,0,0,,He said...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.64,0:16:07.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Speak!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.89,0:16:14.80,Default,,0,0,0,,He said...he said that you have been arrogant and spoke of the Emperor with contempt,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.80,0:16:18.36,Default,,0,0,0,,that you would usurp His Majesty one day.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.89,0:16:22.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is Gou An?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.74,0:16:27.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Gou An fled from Chengdu for Wei long ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.86,0:16:34.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I punished Gou An for delivering supplies too late.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.03,0:16:36.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Hence, he held a grudge and surrendered to Wei.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.93,0:16:41.91,Default,,0,0,0,,It must have been Sima Yi who sent him to spread rumors.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.45,0:16:46.55,Default,,0,0,0,,You are close to His Majesty, yet you spread lies with more lies,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.55,0:16:49.84,Default,,0,0,0,,confusing His Majesty and sabotaging my military plans!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.26,0:16:54.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Harboring such a traitor in court will bring about calamity.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.37,0:17:02.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty! Your Majesty, please spare me!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.85,0:17:07.92,Default,,0,0,0,,At your mercy, Father-Chancellor. At your mercy.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.92,0:17:10.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty! Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.53,0:17:12.23,Default,,0,0,0,,-Guards?\N-Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.23,0:17:13.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor! Chancellor, mercy-
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.82,0:17:15.37,Default,,0,0,0,,-Execute him!\N-Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.37,0:17:18.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.80,0:17:33.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope that all the court officials will detect treachery,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.13,0:17:37.80,Default,,0,0,0,,remonstrate with the Son of Heaven, and aid my Northern Expeditions.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.80,0:17:38.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.18,0:17:42.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.17,0:17:48.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I shall return to Hanzhong immediately and plan an attack against Wei once more.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.54,0:17:50.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Take care.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.19,0:18:20.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, Zhuge Liang leads an army towards Mount Qi once again!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.11,0:18:24.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Wang Ping and Zhang Yi have left Chencang and are coming towards Xie Gorge by San Pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.43,0:18:39.62,Default,,0,0,0,,The wheat is ripe for harvest. Zhuge Liang has come a long way.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.62,0:18:43.48,Default,,0,0,0,,He will certainly cut the wheat of Longxi to bolster his supplies.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.32,0:18:46.13,Default,,0,0,0,,-General Zhang He.\N-Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.13,0:18:49.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Lead forty thousand troops to defend Mount Qi.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.69,0:18:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,I shall patrol Tianshui commandery with \NGeneral Guo to prevent the Shu from harvesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.26,0:18:58.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Grain is running out in the camps, and I have sent for more many times.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.85,0:19:03.47,Default,,0,0,0,,But Li Yan's supplies are still not here, and we cannot afford to wait any longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.32,0:19:06.83,Default,,0,0,0,,The grain in the Longxi Highlands has ripened;
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.83,0:19:10.23,Default,,0,0,0,,men can be sent there to harvest it in secret.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.23,0:19:11.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.42,0:19:13.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps Sima Yi is prepared already.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.38,0:19:15.58,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,3820,4180)\pos(992,461.714)}Jiāng Wéi\NStyled: Bóyuē
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.84,0:19:16.90,Default,,0,0,0,,What should we do if the Wei army is guarding it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.90,0:19:20.11,Default,,0,0,0,,How can there be no grain when battle approaches?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.20,0:19:24.64,Default,,0,0,0,,The wheat in Longxi must be harvested somehow.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.11,0:19:37.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Be vigilant, prevent the Shu army from seizing the wheat.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.68,0:19:41.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I shall make camp here.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.97,0:19:45.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Should Zhuge Liang come, let him be buried here.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.27,0:19:57.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I, Yan Ze, Administrator of Lucheng, welcome the Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.52,0:20:01.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Please rise.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.78,0:20:03.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.00,0:20:06.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Administrator Yan, it is fortunate that you submitted to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.03,0:20:08.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I shall memorialize His Majesty to ask for a quick reward.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.67,0:20:10.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.55,0:20:12.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Is the wheat at Longxi ripe for harvest?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.70,0:20:14.65,Default,,0,0,0,,It can be harvested in a day or two,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.65,0:20:19.34,Default,,0,0,0,,but Sima Yi camped his army next to the fields.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.34,0:20:22.44,Default,,0,0,0,,If the Wei army took all the wheat,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.44,0:20:26.27,Default,,0,0,0,,how will the people of Lucheng live?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.81,0:20:33.50,Default,,0,0,0,,The people need food, and the wheat must not fall into Sima Yi's hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.50,0:20:36.51,Default,,0,0,0,,The Shu army will only take the amount the grain tax dictates.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.51,0:20:41.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope that you make this clear to the people to prevent civil unrest.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.73,0:20:46.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, rest assured. The people of Lucheng has always revered you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.85,0:20:49.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Paying taxes and sending grain are their duties.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.49,0:20:53.98,Default,,0,0,0,,How many soldiers did Sima Yi bring?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.98,0:20:55.44,Default,,0,0,0,,One hundred thousand.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.47,0:21:06.74,Default,,0,0,0,,I have only brought thirty thousand.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.74,0:21:07.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Thirty thousand!?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.15,0:21:14.19,Default,,0,0,0,,-Do you have a map of the Longxi Highlands?\N-Yes, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.66,0:21:32.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Why is this place named "Grove of Strange Trees"?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.31,0:21:37.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, that grove is in treacherous terrain, and strange trees grow there.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.42,0:21:41.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Passersby have often heard of odd sounds emanating from the grove.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.40,0:21:43.82,Default,,0,0,0,,That is why it is named "Grove of Strange Trees."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.68,0:21:48.27,Default,,0,0,0,,But actually, the wind blowing through the trees makes the noise.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.27,0:21:49.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, no need to worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.10,0:21:55.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I will devise a ruse with this grove.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.88,0:21:58.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is Sima Yi camped?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.68,0:22:00.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Not too far from the Grove of Strange Trees.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.83,0:22:07.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Heaven has granted me success!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.24,0:22:16.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, soldiers have been spotted before the camp.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.64,0:22:18.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Not sure if they are men or ghosts.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.12,0:22:20.21,Default,,0,0,0,,They are coming towards our camp.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.79,0:22:45.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander, are these men or monsters?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.70,0:22:53.37,Default,,0,0,0,,As I see it, this must be Zhuge Liang's work again.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.73,0:22:59.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Take two thousand men, capture the men and cart, and bring them here.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.48,0:23:02.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.81,0:23:37.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Men or monsters, capture them first! Let us go!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.62,0:23:52.10,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,5100,5460)\pos(320.667,469.333)}Guō Huái\NStyled: Bójì
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.69,0:23:52.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Those who do not advance will be executed! Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:12.72,0:24:13.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry! Hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:20.54,0:24:22.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry! Hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:22.94,0:24:25.86,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,2500,2900)\pos(670.666,590)}Grove of Strange Trees
Dialogue: 0,0:24:52.12,0:24:55.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Go with me; Zhuge Liang must be captured alive!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:55.69,0:24:56.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:04.54,0:25:06.61,Default,,0,0,0,,General, General, we can't catch up!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:08.70,0:25:10.86,Default,,0,0,0,,If you dare not go forward, how can you catch up?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.86,0:25:13.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Does Zhuge Liang know how to shrink the ground?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.90,0:25:17.70,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Shrinking the ground (缩地): A mythical technique of Taoist origin. It involves shrinking the "Earthly meridians" and allows the user to hide into the ground or warp through the land.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:13.77,0:25:16.68,Default,,0,0,0,,We haven't been able to catch up all day, let's go back!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:16.68,0:25:21.42,Default,,0,0,0,,The insolence! How dare you disobey \Nthe Commander's orders! After them!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:40.46,0:25:43.62,Default,,0,0,0,,These are treacherous grounds. \N Watch out for a Shu ambush.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:44.85,0:25:48.16,Default,,0,0,0,,General Guo is straight ahead; he hasn't caught up to Zhuge Liang.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:48.82,0:25:50.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Give chase!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:22.33,0:26:24.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander, Zhuge Liang is straight ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:28.91,0:26:30.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are you not chasing him down?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:30.93,0:26:33.66,Default,,0,0,0,,We've been chasing him down, yet we can't reach him.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:40.56,0:26:42.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander, how strange!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.02,0:26:45.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Could it be ghosts and spirits that are leading the way?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:47.59,0:26:49.86,Default,,0,0,0,,How could there be ghosts and spirits here?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:07.36,0:27:08.96,Default,,0,0,0,,What kind of noise is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:10.52,0:27:11.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I do not know.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:13.63,0:27:15.52,Default,,0,0,0,,What is the name of this place?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:15.52,0:27:18.67,Default,,0,0,0,,"Grove of Strange Trees." \NRumor has it that demons show up here.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:18.67,0:27:19.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Grove of Strange Trees?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:21.11,0:27:24.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Pass my order, believe not in spirits or devils.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:24.66,0:27:29.02,Default,,0,0,0,,But this is hostile terrain, we cannot stay here. Return at once!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:29.02,0:27:30.03,Default,,0,0,0,,-Yes, sir!\N-Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:34.97,0:27:36.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhuge Liang is here also!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:36.81,0:27:38.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Demons! There are demons!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:52.87,0:27:54.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Retreat! Retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:18.06,0:28:19.22,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(997,446.333)}Jiāng Wéi\NStyled: Bōyuē
Dialogue: 0,0:28:19.22,0:28:20.46,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(989,470)}Mǎ Dài
Dialogue: 0,0:28:20.46,0:28:21.62,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(306,482.333)}Wèi Yán\NStyled: Wéncháng
Dialogue: 0,0:28:22.09,0:28:24.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Sima Yi couldn't figure out whether we were men or ghosts.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:24.43,0:28:26.98,Default,,0,0,0,,He fled to Shanggui and shut the doors behind him!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:27.73,0:28:31.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Such a trivial trick is only a last resort.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:31.50,0:28:34.20,Default,,0,0,0,,It can only fool Sima Yi for the time being.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:35.25,0:28:36.70,Default,,0,0,0,,How is the wheat of Longxi?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:36.70,0:28:41.47,Default,,0,0,0,,While we were dealing with Sima Yi, the troops had collected all the wheat on the Longxi Highlands.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:41.97,0:28:43.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Good! Good!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:43.81,0:28:47.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry and send the wheat to Lucheng for threshing and drying.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:47.85,0:28:48.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:54.19,0:28:57.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Fake Zhuge Liangs pretended to be ghosts and spirits.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:57.63,0:29:04.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet, they still stalled our army of thousands and \Nstole the wheat with a couple of dressed-up men.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:04.61,0:29:07.68,Default,,0,0,0,,This is a complete humiliation!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:08.86,0:29:10.29,Default,,0,0,0,,A humiliation!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:10.94,0:29:16.18,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,4900,5220)\pos(989,498)}Sūn Lǐ\NStyled: Dédá
Dialogue: 0,0:29:10.51,0:29:13.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Worry not. I have brought the troops of Yong and Liang Provinces.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:13.71,0:29:17.12,Default,,0,0,0,,They can just be sent to Lucheng and take the wheat back for you, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:21.12,0:29:26.80,Default,,0,0,0,,General Sun, you must take Lucheng and its wheat supply immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:26.80,0:29:30.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Whether or not we can repel the Shu army depends on this.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:30.86,0:29:32.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Commander, rest assured!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:53.96,0:29:55.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Charge!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:12.00,0:30:16.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold! Hold!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:19.94,0:30:23.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Give chase! Give chase! Hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:33.10,0:30:34.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:35.39,0:30:39.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, we have achieved victory without a single casualty.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:40.12,0:30:42.28,Default,,0,0,0,,This is all due to your miraculous plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:42.28,0:30:46.83,Default,,0,0,0,,No, this is all due to our men's bravery in battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:46.83,0:30:51.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Following this victory, you can go back home and reunite with your families.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:52.96,0:30:56.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, Guardian-General Li Yan has an urgent message.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:03.09,0:31:06.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, is this about the supplies?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:07.76,0:31:11.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Li Yan reports that Wu has allied with Wei,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:11.93,0:31:14.39,Default,,0,0,0,,and that they intend to trespass our borders.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:16.93,0:31:21.37,Thinking,,0,0,0,,In the 9th year of the Jianxing Era of Shu-Han (231 CE),
Dialogue: 0,0:31:21.37,0:31:23.63,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Zhuge Liang set out of Mount Qi for the fifth time.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:23.63,0:31:26.83,Thinking,,0,0,0,,He used a ruse to harvest all the wheat of the Longxi Highlands,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:26.83,0:31:30.17,Thinking,,0,0,0,,then defeated the Wei army at Lucheng.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:30.17,0:31:32.84,Thinking,,0,0,0,,While he was in the city to congratulate the troops,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:32.84,0:31:38.61,Thinking,,0,0,0,,a sudden report from Li Yan in Yong'an came, saying that Wu would attack Shu.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:38.61,0:31:40.53,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Zhuge Liang withdrew in a hurry.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:40.53,0:31:45.72,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Upon hearing this, Sima Yi sent Vanguard General Zhang He to give chase.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:40.53,0:31:41.15,Default,,0,0,0,,-Retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:46.06,0:31:52.29,Thinking,,0,0,0,,When he was passing through Mumen Path, Zhang He was shot to death by the Shu soldiers.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:49.12,0:31:51.86,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(318,427.667)}Fèi Yì\NStyled: Wénwěi
Dialogue: 0,0:31:57.71,0:31:59.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:59.61,0:32:01.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief-Clerk Fei.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:03.28,0:32:06.56,Default,,0,0,0,,I come here on His Majesty the Son of Heaven's orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:06.56,0:32:10.21,Default,,0,0,0,,His Majesty asks why you have withdrawn to Hanzhong.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:12.32,0:32:18.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Li Yan sent an urgent message saying that Eastern Wu is attacking the Riverlands.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:18.17,0:32:24.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Thus, I withdrew the army. How does the Son of Heaven not know of this?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:31.09,0:32:32.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Li Yan met with His Majesty,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:32.74,0:32:37.86,Default,,0,0,0,,saying that he worked very hard to gather supplies and that they are now ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:37.86,0:32:40.77,Default,,0,0,0,,The Son of Heaven praised him profusely for this.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:40.77,0:32:42.66,Default,,0,0,0,,With the news of your withdrawal,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:42.66,0:32:45.18,Default,,0,0,0,,His Majesty has ordered me to come to inquiry.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:01.31,0:33:04.91,Default,,0,0,0,,That ignoramus Li Yan was falling short of amassing supplies,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:04.91,0:33:08.24,Default,,0,0,0,,so he made up such a lie to cover up his mistake!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:10.48,0:33:15.24,Default,,0,0,0,,He fooled me into coming to Hanzhong! \NThe nerve of him to lie to both sides!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:19.64,0:33:25.04,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,As an official entrusted with guardianship, \Nhe damaged the dynasty's cause for his own gain!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:25.04,0:33:28.99,Default,,0,0,0,,How can this be acceptable?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.00,0:33:34.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, the late emperor did entrust him with guardianship after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:34.76,0:33:40.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Please think carefully on how to deal with this matter!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:44.70,0:33:52.22,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,7000,7500)\pos(930,499.333)}Lǐ Yán\NStyled: Zhèngfāng
Dialogue: 0,0:33:47.63,0:33:55.38,Default,,0,0,0,,The Emperor has sent Fei Yi to Hanzhong. The plot has been exposed.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:56.43,0:33:59.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Would the Chancellor let us off lightly?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:01.70,0:34:07.53,Default,,0,0,0,,My son Feng, it is I who got you into trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:03.06,0:34:08.06,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(1001,477)}Lǐ Fēng\NStyled: Guó'ān
Dialogue: 0,0:34:11.18,0:34:16.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I, Li Yan, cannot face the late emperor...
Dialogue: 0,0:34:18.45,0:34:20.81,Default,,0,0,0,,my forebears...
Dialogue: 0,0:34:22.85,0:34:25.85,Default,,0,0,0,,...and my family!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:26.19,0:34:29.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Father... Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:30.06,0:34:33.81,Default,,0,0,0,,It has been found out that Li Yan could not gather enough supplies,
Dialogue: 0,0:34:33.81,0:34:37.64,Default,,0,0,0,,and so feared the Chancellor's rebuke and forged an edict to recall him.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:37.64,0:34:39.89,Default,,0,0,0,,This caused the Chancellor's army to retreat.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:39.89,0:34:42.73,Default,,0,0,0,,He also dared to petition Your Majesty to cover up his faults.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:43.81,0:34:46.67,Default,,0,0,0,,How dare Li Yan fool Us!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:46.67,0:34:50.68,Default,,0,0,0,,He even forged an imperial edict to recall and ruin Father-Chancellor's work!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:50.68,0:34:53.77,Default,,0,0,0,,How can Our hatred be satiated without killing his family?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:53.77,0:34:54.42,Default,,0,0,0,,We decree!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:54.42,0:34:55.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:56.38,0:34:58.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty! Wait, Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:58.91,0:35:02.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, when I went to Hanzhong,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:02.26,0:35:06.40,Default,,0,0,0,,the Chancellor, recognizing that Li Yan was entrusted with guardianship,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:06.49,0:35:10.35,Default,,0,0,0,,voiced hopes that Your Majesty would resolve this prudently.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:10.35,0:35:14.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Then... what is Father-Chancellor's opinion?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:14.20,0:35:19.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, the Chancellor asked me to plead with Your Majesty
Dialogue: 0,0:35:19.31,0:35:23.22,Default,,0,0,0,,to reduce Li Yan to a commoner and banish him to Zitong Commandery,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:23.22,0:35:30.16,Default,,0,0,0,,and that his son, Li Feng, would replace him and oversee the transport of supplies northward.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:30.16,0:35:34.45,Default,,0,0,0,,His crime is such that death would be too merciful! How could we let his son succeed him?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:34.45,0:35:38.40,Default,,0,0,0,,The Chancellor said that Li Yan knows that his crime is serious.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:38.40,0:35:41.93,Default,,0,0,0,,If Your Majesty reduced his sentence, he would be grateful.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:41.93,0:35:45.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Doing so can avoid a future disaster. This is the first advantage.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:45.84,0:35:50.48,Default,,0,0,0,,If you have his son succeed him, who will do his best to amass supplies,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:50.48,0:35:53.61,Default,,0,0,0,,this will resolve the logistics issue. This is the second advantage.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:53.61,0:35:59.44,Default,,0,0,0,,After succeeding, Li Feng will avoid his father's mistakes and not dare hinder major affairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:59.44,0:36:01.04,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the third advantage.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:01.04,0:36:04.42,Default,,0,0,0,,There are three advantages:\N what arguments are there against them?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:05.19,0:36:09.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Good! Good! We shall follow Father-Chancellor's advice and spare Li Yan.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:09.44,0:36:13.56,Default,,0,0,0,,We decree to remove Li Yan from his position and demote him to a commoner.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:13.56,0:36:17.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Banish him to Zitong Commandery and appoint his son Li Feng as Chief-Clerk.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:17.68,0:36:20.67,Default,,0,0,0,,He shall gather supplies and be on his way immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:20.67,0:36:21.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:29.95,0:36:32.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Feng, my son, Feng!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:32.76,0:36:36.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Father, I have prepared the rations,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:36.06,0:36:38.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I am departing for Hanzhong soon. Why have you come, Father?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:38.86,0:36:42.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Feng, the Emperor showed mercy to our family
Dialogue: 0,0:36:42.92,0:36:45.55,Default,,0,0,0,,because the Chancellor has spoken for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:45.55,0:36:50.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I will go to Hanzhong with you and apologize to the Chancellor personally.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:50.66,0:36:51.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:52.60,0:36:56.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Quit talking! If it wasn't for the Chancellor,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:56.70,0:37:00.24,Default,,0,0,0,,we would have become slain ghosts.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:00.24,0:37:03.89,Default,,0,0,0,,How would we have the honors that we have today?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:03.89,0:37:06.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Come, bind your father.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:07.22,0:37:08.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Father, this-
Dialogue: 0,0:37:08.45,0:37:09.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Why won't you do it now?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:13.12,0:37:16.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Father, I dare not.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:16.34,0:37:21.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you want your father to kneel before you and beg?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:24.22,0:37:26.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Father! Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:40.62,0:37:45.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, I have been honing our strength for three years.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:45.95,0:37:48.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Now our supply is ample and our arms are plenty.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:48.99,0:37:52.75,Default,,0,0,0,,With strong troops, an attack against Wei is now feasible.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:54.07,0:37:59.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Until I conquer the wicked\N and recover the Central Plains,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:59.51,0:38:03.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I will not come back to see Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:08.65,0:38:13.91,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Dǐng (鼎): an ancient Chinese cauldron with three legs, made of bronze. \NTraditionally seen as a symbol for power and authority.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:08.65,0:38:13.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Father-Chancellor, the realm has been stable like the legs of a {\i1}ding{\i0} cauldron,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:13.91,0:38:16.91,Default,,0,0,0,,and Wu and Wei have not invaded.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:16.91,0:38:20.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Father-Chancellor, why not enjoy the peace?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:20.29,0:38:23.14,Default,,0,0,0,,For the kindness of the late emperor's patronage,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:23.14,0:38:28.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I have never stopped dreaming\N about fighting Wei to restore the Han.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:28.96,0:38:35.74,Default,,0,0,0,,I have done my utmost in loyalty to restore the Central Plains for Your Majesty and restore the Han.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:35.74,0:38:38.15,Default,,0,0,0,,This is my wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:38.15,0:38:44.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, in my humble opinion, the Chancellor must not send troops!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:38.26,0:38:43.46,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,4860,5180)\pos(993,498.667)}Qiáo Zhōu\NStyled: Yǔnnán
Dialogue: 0,0:38:44.78,0:38:48.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, I am in charge of the Bureau of Astronomy.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:48.48,0:38:53.04,Default,,0,0,0,,There is an inauspicious sign today, and I fear that this would be bad for our army.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:53.04,0:38:57.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}Celestial signs are but mirages and fantasies. How can they be evidence?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:57.15,0:39:02.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}Your Majesty, we have set forth from Mount Qi five times, none of which has been effective.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:02.07,0:39:05.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord9\pos(640,670)}Clearly the time to destroy Wei has not come yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:05.64,0:39:08.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}The Shu army has been fighting constantly.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:08.20,0:39:13.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}The fires of war have not been extinguished and arduous paths have been trudged many times.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:13.09,0:39:16.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}Our national strength and \Npopular support will be sapped.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:16.26,0:39:18.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}Another expedition out of Mount Qi now
Dialogue: 0,0:39:18.69,0:39:24.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}would have no favors from Heaven, Earth, and mankind.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:24.03,0:39:27.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}I hope that the Chancellor will judge the situation wisely
Dialogue: 0,0:39:27.12,0:39:32.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}and do not do anything that should not be done.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:34.58,0:39:38.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}Palace Attendant Dong's words are not without reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:38.64,0:39:42.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}We hope that Father-Chancellor will think carefully.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:42.00,0:39:46.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}Your Majesty, I was entrusted by the late emperor with guardianship.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:46.44,0:39:48.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord9\pos(640,670)}I shall fight the traitors,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:48.44,0:39:53.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}and I will have no regrets, \Neven if I were to die nine times!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:53.88,0:39:57.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}If we loiter in Shu and wait for \NWu and Wei to enter the Riverlands,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:57.58,0:40:05.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}how could I ever face the\N late emperor in the afterlife?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:12.27,0:40:16.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord9\pos(640,670)}Now spring is here, the season of war.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:16.99,0:40:22.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}Before I depart, I will make a sacrifice to the temple of the late emperor,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:22.30,0:40:25.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}and ask for blessings from his esteemed spirit;
Dialogue: 0,0:40:25.22,0:40:28.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13\pos(640,670)}this will turn peril into safety.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:29.36,0:40:36.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13}After I go, I will fight to the death, so that Cao-Wei can be defeated.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:39.10,0:40:43.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Good. Father-Chancellor, We shall, according to your intent...
Dialogue: 0,0:40:45.74,0:40:48.73,Default,,0,0,0,,begin the Northern Expedition immediately.
Comment: 0,0:10:14.47,0:10:21.34,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,There are two historical mistakes here. Firstly, "Last Lord" (后主) was a name used by later historians. Secondly, directly referring to Liu Shan by his name would be violating naming taboo.
Comment: 0,0:34:03.06,0:34:09.16,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: This style name belonged to a Wei minister also named Li Feng. This is a historical mistake.

